<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · disaster</p><h1 class="enc-title">COVID-19 pandemic</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2019">2019</a>–<a href="/years/2023">2023</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as coronavirus pandemic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The COVID-19 pandemic was a global outbreak of the disease caused by the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus, first identified in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wuhan">Wuhan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, in December 2019. Declared a pandemic by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-health-organization">World Health Organization</a> in March 2020, it caused millions of deaths, lockdowns and border closures worldwide and a severe economic shock. Mass vaccination from 2021 reduced its toll, and the WHO ended the global health emergency in May 2023.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/covid-19-pandemic.jpg" alt="COVID-19 pandemic" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gustavo Basso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Covid-19_SP_-_UTI_V._Nova_Cachoeirinha.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
